### identity on your PC (Lab 4) - start it first:  cd services/identity && npm run dev
### Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension and click "Send Request".
### For requests that need a token: sign in with identity/requests.http first and paste the accessToken.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@token = PASTE-ACCESS-TOKEN-HERE

### Health -> 200, runtime pc
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### Register a member -> 201 (role is always member)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Laila Hassan", "email": "laila.{{$randomInt 1000 9999}}@example.com", "password": "StrongPass2026" }

### Register with bad data and a "role" field -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "X", "email": "nope", "password": "short", "role": "admin" }

### Sign in -> 200 + accessToken (e-mail/password from infra/.generated/seed-credentials.txt)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ali.member@gym.local", "password": "PASTE-FROM-seed-credentials.txt" }

### Wrong password -> 401 with a generic message
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ali.member@gym.local", "password": "WrongPassword1" }

### My profile -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Not JSON -> 415
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: text/plain

hello
